# Both CAN Triple repositories (the firmware and the Device Manager GUI)
# disable ALL end-of-line normalization: every file is committed byte-exact
# and must check out byte-exact.
#
# In the GUI repo the reasons are concrete:
#   - installer/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt is deliberately CRLF and pure ASCII,
#     and is fed verbatim to Inno Setup's InfoAfterFile — the installer shows
#     and ships the literal bytes.
#   - COPYING and the licence texts under installer/ are verbatim licence
#     documents; their bytes are not ours to rewrite.
#   - installer/CANTripleDeviceManager.iss is encoding-sensitive.
#
# A clone that CRLF-normalized on checkout (or LF-normalized on commit) would
# corrupt all of them, so EOL handling is switched off wholesale rather than
# guarded per-file, and the firmware repo mirrors the policy so the pair of
# checkouts always behaves the same way.
* -text
